      "category_hint": "Christmas ornaments (Home & Garden > Holiday & Seasonal Decor > Christmas Ornaments); resolve the Bonanza/eBay category id with getCategories",
      "description": "<p>Four Christmas ornaments, each one a famous fractal: shapes that repeat themselves at smaller and smaller scales.</p><ul><li><b>Koch snowflake (1904):</b> a triangle gets a smaller triangle on the middle of every edge, again and again. Its edge grows without end, yet its area stays under 8/5 of the first triangle. Raised lines on the face show steps 0, 1 and 2.</li><li><b>Sierpinski triangle (1915)</b>, shaped as a little tree: take out the middle triangle, then repeat in the three that are left.</li><li><b>Pythagoras tree (1942):</b> every square carries two smaller squares, and their areas always add up to the one below, a² + b² = c².</li><li><b>Pentaflake:</b> a pentagon made of six pentagons, each made of six more, shrinking by the golden ratio.</li></ul><p>Two sets: Classic (white snowflake, green tree, red Pythagoras tree, gold pentaflake) or All gold.</p><ul><li>Set of 4 flat ornaments, each about 5.7 to 7.7 cm (2.2 to 3 in) tall and 3.5 mm thick</li><li>Each has a 4 mm hole for a ribbon, thread or hook; hanging cord not included</li><li>About 37 g for all four; PLA, printed layer by layer, so fine layer lines show up close</li><li>Designed by us and printed to order in the USA</li><li>Decorative only: not a toy, keep away from small children and from heat above 50 °C (120 °F)</li></ul><p>The photos are digital renders made from the real print files. Colours can vary a little between filament batches.</p>",
